   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "הַשּׂוֹנֵא כֹּל שֶׁלֹּא דִּבֵּר כּוּ׳. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: ״וְהוּא לֹא אוֹיֵב לוֹ״ – יְעִידֶנּוּ, ״וְלֹא מְבַקֵּשׁ רָעָתוֹ״ – יְדִינֶנּוּ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «One who hates» the litigant is referring to «anyone» who, out of enmity, «did not speak» with the litigant for three days. «The Sages taught» in a baraita: This halakha is derived from the verse: “And he was not his enemy, neither sought his harm” (Numbers 35:23), that one about whom it can be stated: «“And he was not his enemy,” can testify about him.» And one who «“neither sought his harm” can judge him.»"
  }
 ],
